ENTRY 12312 {"id":12312,"kind":"pi.tool-result","messages":[{"role":"toolResult","text":"     1\t# One replica, Recreate: the Postgres adapter allows a single owner per schema.\n     2\t# Code comes from the orchestrator-code PVC (deploy/push-code.sh), so no image is pushed.\n     3\t# The DB URI comes from the CNPG-generated secret pi-pg-app and is never printed.\n     4\tapiVersion: apps/v1\n     5\tkind: Deployment\n     6\tmetadata:\n     7\t  name: pi-orchestrator\n     8\t  labels:\n     9\t    app.kubernetes.io/name: pi-orchestrator\n    10\tspec:\n    11\t  replicas: 1\n    12\t  strategy:\n    13\t    type: Recreate\n    14\t  selector:\n    15\t    matchLabels:\n    16\t      app.kubernetes.io/name: pi-orchestrator\n    17\t      app.kubernetes.io/instance: pi-orchestrator\n    18\t  template:\n    19\t    metadata:\n    20\t      labels:\n    21\t        app.kubernetes.io/name: pi-orchestrator\n    22\t        app.kubernetes.io/instance: pi-orchestrator\n    23\t    spec:\n    24\t      serviceAccountName: pi-orchestrator\n    25\t      securityContext:\n    26\t        runAsNonRoot: true\n    27\t        runAsUser: 1000\n    28\t        runAsGroup: 1000\n    29\t        fsGroup: 1000\n    30\t        seccompProfile:\n    31\t          type: RuntimeDefault\n    32\t      containers:\n    33\t        - name: orchestrator\n    34\t          image: node:22-bookworm-slim\n    35\t          workingDir: /code/app\n    36\t          command: [node, dist/main.js]\n    37\t          # PI_MODEL_PROVIDER, PI_MODEL_ID, PI_MODEL_ALLOWLIST, PI_SESSION_TURN_BUDGET.\n    38\t          envFrom:\n    39\t            - configMapRef: { name: pi-model-config }\n    40\t          env:\n    41\t            - { name: HOME, value: /tmp }\n    42\t            - { name: PI_ORCH_NAMESPACE, value: pi-durable-poc }\n    43\t            - { name: PI_ORCH_WARMPOOL, value: pi-env-pool }\n    44\t            - { name: PI_ORCH_PORT, value: \"8081\" }\n    45\t            - { name: PI_DURABLE_SCHEMA, value: durable }\n    46\t            - name: POD_NAME\n    47\t              valueFrom: { fieldRef: { fieldPath: metadata.name } }\n    48\t            - name: PI_DURABLE_DATABASE_URL\n    49\t              valueFrom: { secretKeyRef: { name: pi-pg-app, key: uri } }\n    50\t            # Master key of the per-sandbox sandboxd tokens: HMAC(master, claim). Never reaches a bridge or a sandbox.\n    51\t            - name: PI_SANDBOX_MASTER_KEY\n    52\t              valueFrom: { secretKeyRef: { name: sandboxd-auth, key: master } }\n    53\t            # Same bearer tokens as ingest (create with deploy/gen-api-secret.sh): the stream endpoint\n    54\t            # authenticates the caller again and checks the session owner.\n    55\t            - name: PI_API_TOKENS\n    56\t              valueFrom: { secretKeyRef: { name: api-auth, key: tokens } }\n    57\t            # Model calls go through the OneCLI gateway with this agent token (an ExternalSecret from secret-store,\n    58\t            # deploy/onecli-externalsecret.yaml). Optional so the scripted model runs without it. It is read from the\n    59\t            # environment once and never logged; bridge-launcher strips it from every bridge child.\n    60\t            - name: ONECLI_AGENT_TOKEN\n    61\t              valueFrom: { secretKeyRef: { name: pi-onecli, key: agent-token, optional: true } }\n    62\t            # Phase 4c: management API key for per-session OneCLI agents (repo sessions only; optional).\n    63\t            - name: ONECLI_API_KEY\n    64\t              valueFrom: { secretKeyRef: { name: pi-onecli-admin, key: api-key, optional: true } }\n    65\t            - { name: PI_ONECLI_API, value: \"http://onecli.onecli:10256\" }\n    66\t            - { name: PI_ONECLI_GATEWAY, value: \"http://onecli.onecli:10255\" }\n    67\t            - { name: PI_ONECLI_CA_FILE, value: /etc/onecli/ca.pem }\n    68\t            # No process-wide HTTPS_PROXY: only pi-ai's model calls use a dispatcher scoped to the gateway. NO_PROXY\n    69\t            # is the belt and braces list (cluster, Kubernetes API, Postgres) the orchestrator also applies itself.\n    70\t            - { name: NO_PROXY, value: \"localhost,127.0.0.1,.svc,.cluster.local,kubernetes.default,pi-pg-rw,10.0.0.0/8\" }\n    71\t            # Test-only, both off unless set. CONTROL mounts the authenticated Phase 3 scripted-session surface\n    72\t            # under /control. TEST_FAULTS honours payload.testFault on inbox rows, which only SQL can write\n    73\t            # (ingest never does), so the Phase 4 suite can kill the orchestrator between submit and mark.\n    74\t          ports:\n    75\t            - { name: control, containerPort: 8081 }\n    76\t          readinessProbe:\n    77\t            httpGet: { path: /readyz, port: control }\n    78\t            periodSeconds: 3\n    79\t          resources:\n    80\t            requests: { cpu: 100m, memory: 256Mi }\n    81\t            limits: { cpu: \"1\", memory: 2Gi }\n    82\t          securityContext:\n    83\t            allowPrivilegeEscalation: false\n    84\t            capabilities:\n    85\t              drop: [ALL]\n    86\t          volumeMounts:\n    87\t            - { name: code, mountPath: /code, readOnly: true }\n    88\t            - { name: onecli-ca, mountPath: /etc/onecli, readOnly: true }\n    89\t            - { name: github-app, mountPath: /etc/pi-github-app, readOnly: true }\n    90\t      volumes:\n    91\t        # GitHub App key for minting per-repo tokens (ExternalSecret pi-github-app); optional like the CA.\n    92\t        - name: github-app\n    93\t          secret: { secretName: pi-github-app, optional: true }\n    94\t        # Filled by deploy/fetch-onecli-ca.sh; optional so the scripted model starts without it.\n    95\t        - name: onecli-ca\n    96\t          configMap: { name: onecli-ca, optional: true }\n    97\t        - name: code\n    98\t          persistentVolumeClaim:\n    99\t            claimName: orchestrator-code\n     1\t# Holds the bundled orchestrator code so a pod restart keeps it. Filled by deploy/push-code.sh.\n     2\tapiVersion: v1\n     3\tkind: PersistentVolumeClaim\n     4\tmetadata:\n     5\t  name: orchestrator-code\n     6\tspec:\n     7\t  accessModes: [ReadWriteOnce]\n     8\t  storageClassName: longhorn-static\n     9\t  resources:\n    10\t    requests:\n    11\t      storage: 1Gi\n/bin/bash: line 1: rg: command not found\n     1\t#!/usr/bin/env bash\n     2\t# Bundle ingest (with its workspace dependency session-core) into ConfigMap `ingest-code`, which the\n     3\t# pi-ingest Deployment unpacks in an initContainer. No image is built or pushed. Restarts the pods when the\n     4\t# bundle changed. Usage: deploy/push-ingest.sh\n     5\tset -euo pipefail\n     6\t\n     7\tctx=${KUBE_CONTEXT:-}\n     8\tns=${NAMESPACE:-pi-durable-poc}\n     9\there=$(cd \"$(dirname \"$0\")\" && pwd)\n    10\troot=$(cd \"$here/..\" && pwd)\n    11\twork=$(mktemp -d)\n    12\tk() { kubectl ${ctx:+--context=\"$ctx\"} -n \"$ns\" \"$@\"; }\n    13\ttrap 'rm -rf \"$work\"' EXIT\n    14\t\n    15\t(cd \"$root\" && pnpm install --frozen-lockfile >/dev/null && pnpm --filter @pi-durable-k8s/session-core --filter @pi-durable-k8s/ingest build >/dev/null)\n    16\t(cd \"$root\" && pnpm --filter @pi-durable-k8s/ingest deploy --prod \"$work/app\" >/dev/null)\n    17\tCOPYFILE_DISABLE=1 tar --no-xattrs -czf \"$work/app.tgz\" -C \"$work/app\" .\n    18\tsize=$(wc -c <\"$work/app.tgz\" | tr -d ' ')\n    19\tif [[ $size -gt 900000 ]]; then\n    20\t  echo \"ingest bundle is $size bytes; a ConfigMap holds 1 MiB. Switch to a code PVC (see deploy/ingest.yaml).\" >&2\n    21\t  exit 1\n    22\tfi\n    23\t\n    24\tsum=$(shasum -a 256 \"$work/app.tgz\" | awk '{print $1}')\n    25\tcurrent=$(k get configmap ingest-code -o jsonpath='{.metadata.annotations.bundle-sha256}' 2>/dev/null || true)\n    26\tif [[ $current == \"$sum\" ]]; then\n    27\t  echo \"ingest bundle unchanged\"\n    28\t  exit 0\n    29\tfi\n    30\tk create configmap ingest-code --from-file=app.tgz=\"$work/app.tgz\" --dry-run=client -o yaml |\n    31\t  k annotate --local -f - \"bundle-sha256=$sum\" -o yaml | k apply -f - >/dev/null\n    32\tif k get deployment pi-ingest >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n    33\t  k rollout restart deployment/pi-ingest >/dev/null\n    34\tfi\n    35\techo \"ingest bundle pushed ($size bytes)\"\n","isError":false}]}
ENTRY 12388 {"id":12388,"kind":"pi.assistant","messages":[{"role":"assistant","text":"[thinking]","calls":["bash({\"command\":\"cd /workspace/repo && sed -n '12,78p' deploy/push-code.sh && grep -R -n 'push-code.sh' README.md deploy scripts 2>/dev/null | head -40\"})"]}]}
ENTRY 12392 {"id":12392,"kind":"pi.tool-result","messages":[{"role":"toolResult","text":"work=$(mktemp -d)\ndeployments=(\"$@\")\n[[ ${#deployments[@]} -gt 0 ]] || deployments=(pi-orchestrator)\nk() { kubectl ${ctx:+--context=\"$ctx\"} -n \"$ns\" \"$@\"; }\nscaled=() # deployments this run scaled to 0; the trap restores exactly these\n# Runs on every exit path: a failed wait, cp or extract must not leave the orchestrator at 0 replicas.\ncleanup() {\n  local d\n  rm -rf \"$work\"\n  k delete pod orchestrator-code-loader --ignore-not-found --wait=false >/dev/null 2>&1 || true\n  for d in ${scaled[@]+\"${scaled[@]}\"}; do\n    k scale deployment \"$d\" --replicas=1 >/dev/null || echo \"could not scale $d back to 1; run: kubectl -n $ns scale deployment $d --replicas=1\" >&2\n  done\n}\ntrap cleanup EXIT\n\n(cd \"$root\" && pnpm install --frozen-lockfile >/dev/null && pnpm --filter \"@pi-durable-k8s/orchestrator...\" build >/dev/null)\n(cd \"$root\" && pnpm --filter @pi-durable-k8s/orchestrator deploy --prod \"$work/app\" >/dev/null)\nCOPYFILE_DISABLE=1 tar --no-xattrs -czf \"$work/app.tgz\" -C \"$work/app\" .\n\nk apply -f \"$here/orchestrator-code-pvc.yaml\" >/dev/null\nfor d in \"${deployments[@]}\"; do\n  if k get deployment \"$d\" >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n    scaled+=(\"$d\")\n    k scale deployment \"$d\" --replicas=0 >/dev/null\n  fi\ndone\nfor d in \"${deployments[@]}\"; do\n  k wait --for=delete pod -l \"app.kubernetes.io/instance=$d\" --timeout=120s >/dev/null 2>&1 || true\ndone\n\nk delete pod orchestrator-code-loader --ignore-not-found --wait=true >/dev/null\nk apply -f - >/dev/null <<EOF\napiVersion: v1\nkind: Pod\nmetadata:\n  name: orchestrator-code-loader\nspec:\n  restartPolicy: Never\n  securityContext: { runAsNonRoot: true, runAsUser: 1000, runAsGroup: 1000, fsGroup: 1000, seccompProfile: { type: RuntimeDefault } }\n  containers:\n    - name: loader\n      image: node:22-bookworm-slim\n      command: [sleep, \"600\"]\n      securityContext: { allowPrivilegeEscalation: false, capabilities: { drop: [ALL] } }\n      resources:\n        requests: { cpu: 10m, memory: 32Mi }\n        limits: { cpu: 100m, memory: 128Mi }\n      volumeMounts: [{ name: code, mountPath: /code }]\n  volumes:\n    - name: code\n      persistentVolumeClaim: { claimName: orchestrator-code }\nEOF\nk wait --for=condition=Ready pod/orchestrator-code-loader --timeout=240s >/dev/null\nk cp \"$work/app.tgz\" orchestrator-code-loader:/tmp/app.tgz >/dev/null\n# Extract beside the live tree and swap only after the entry point exists, so a failed extract leaves the old\n# code in place. Same volume, so each mv is a rename.\nk exec orchestrator-code-loader -- sh -c 'set -e\nrm -rf /code/app.new /code/app.old\nmkdir -p /code/app.new\ntar xzf /tmp/app.tgz -C /code/app.new\nls /code/app.new/dist/main.js >/dev/null\nif [ -e /code/app ]; then mv /code/app /code/app.old; fi\nmv /code/app.new /code/app\nrm -rf /code/app.old'\nk delete pod orchestrator-code-loader --wait=true >/dev/null\n# The EXIT trap scales the deployments back to 1.\ndeploy/orchestrator-code-pvc.yaml:1:# Holds the bundled orchestrator code so a pod restart keeps it. Filled by deploy/push-code.sh.\ndeploy/push-code.sh:5:# Usage: deploy/push-code.sh [deployment...]   (default: pi-orchestrator; scaled back to 1 afterwards)\ndeploy/kustomization.yaml:25:# Secret `pi-pg-app` is generated by CloudNativePG. Fill the code PVC with deploy/push-code.sh.\ndeploy/orchestrator.yaml:2:# Code comes from the orchestrator-code PVC (deploy/push-code.sh), so no image is pushed.\n","isError":false}]}
ENTRY 12422 {"id":12422,"kind":"pi.assistant","messages":[{"role":"assistant","text":"## Findings\n\n### 1. Interrupted swap can leave the orchestrator without code\n- Severity: high\n- Confidence: high\n- Location: deploy/push-code.sh:74\n- What happens: If the loader is killed or the second rename fails after `/code/app` is moved aside, the exit trap restarts the deployment with no `/code/app`. A subsequent push also deletes `/code/app.old` before installing the replacement, losing the previous working copy.\n- Evidence: `mv /code/app /code/app.old` followed by `mv /code/app.new /code/app`\n- Fix idea: Recover any interrupted swap before deleting the backup, and restore the old tree if installation fails. Use an atomic pointer switch between versioned directories to avoid a missing live path.\n\n### 2. Concurrent pushes interfere with each other\n- Severity: high\n- Confidence: high\n- Location: deploy/push-code.sh:21\n- What happens: Two pushes share the same loader pod and staging paths. Either invocation can delete the other’s loader, including when its own build fails before creating a pod; its cleanup can also scale the deployment back up while the other push is still writing.\n- Evidence: `k delete pod orchestrator-code-loader --ignore-not-found --wait=false` runs unconditionally in the exit trap.\n- Fix idea: Serialize pushes with a cluster-scoped lock for the PVC. Make cleanup delete only resources owned by the current invocation.\n\n### 3. Pod deletion wait failures are ignored\n- Severity: medium\n- Confidence: high\n- Location: deploy/push-code.sh:40\n- What happens: If an orchestrator pod takes more than 120 seconds to terminate, or the wait fails for another reason, the script proceeds anyway. The loader can then modify the code volume while the old orchestrator is still running on the same node, or fail to mount it on another node.\n- Evidence: `k wait --for=delete pod ... --timeout=120s >/dev/null 2>&1 || true`\n- Fix idea: Treat failure to confirm pod deletion as a deployment failure and let cleanup restore the deployment without writing the volume.\n\nEND-OF-REPORT"}]}
DONE
